{"kind":"artifact","text":"Directional reviewed-path reach at exact clean pushed head 9fa3d197bcc3065134ab20d22f00dcdba9242f51 on request/directional-reviewed-paths, based on main 6fad9e8a: cmd/gs changes. Republication of stale-at-birth 217b74e3, which I retire beside this filing: that artifact rested on proposal #10515, which my own directed retirement of its parent bundle had just flared — so this filing rests only on the fresh behavior anchors, and the governing decision is cited here in text. GOVERNING DECISION: proposal #10515 (id d6f04538161ff9f18744d4a5630bb3aae379b7cc), \"a reviewed path authorizes cross-author retirement only at itself or beneath it, never above it,\" ratified by hugh at seq 10722 by act 8fa3703c; the ratification stands and the proposal's staleness is ordinary anchor movement from the reconciliation's own directed retirements. The implementing commit's Rests-On trailer names that proposal immutably. THE CHANGE: withinReviewedPaths now runs the same direction as the fold's pathCovers; cmd/gs's single-caller symmetric sameTreeLineage helper is removed; the fold's copy and all accounting behavior (merge_changed_paths, merge_left_live) are untouched. Tests state both allowed directions and the refusal, assert the refusal originates in the command preflight, and the mutation check was run: restoring the symmetric direction fails the refusal test. Gates at this exact head: gofmt clean, vet clean, go test -count=1 across cmd and internal all ok, docset ok re-run after the final edit. TWO AUDIT FINDINGS for the reviewer: the fold's reviewed-to-target comparison in mergeReceiptPlan remains deliberately symmetric, so the command is now strictly narrower than the fold, not aligned with it; and the proposal's stranding scenario is not reachable through planSuccession, whose successors always cover their targets — the real effect is tightened cross-author authority, refusing some merges the fold would have accepted. The ratified sentence authorizes exactly that tightening; its motivating story was partly wrong and this artifact says so.","body":{"branch":"request/directional-reviewed-paths","commit":"9fa3d197bcc3065134ab20d22f00dcdba9242f51","path":"cmd/gs"}}